  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asian Elephant Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to continue activities already started and implemented with support from the USFWS assistance awards no 9-G081A, I-G058 and F12AP00933 to improve Sumatran elephant and other endangered Sumatran wildlife conservation efforts by fulfilling the vital need for the above-mentioned veterinary expertise and services, throughout Sumatra. During this project, immediate support and emergency response will be provided to any government agency or NGO active in elephant and endangered wildlife conservation in Sumatra, in need of veterinary expertise in cases of injured wild elephants, rescue of trapped wild elephants, translocation of elephants, or conducting post-mortems on dead wild elephants. The project will also provide regular veterinary care and on-call emergency response to programs regularly utilizing captive elephants for elephant conservation activities such as patrols in protected elephant habitat, HEC mitigation, local community awareness, conservation education and research programs. Training will be provided to mahouts and staff in such programs about the basics of medical management of elephants, daily health care needs and elephant biology. This will ensure these elephants health and fitness, thus ensuring a continuation of elephant conservation activities.</narrative>
  </description>
